          data-guid="7683308"
    >
(Reserved)    </span>
    </a>
    <span class="titleFootnotes">
        <a id="ref7683308-1"
           href="#ft7683308-1"
           class="footnoteref"
        >
          [1]
        </a>
    </span>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7683308" data-guid="7683308"></div>
        <div id="questions-7683308" data-guid="7683308" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7683308_content" title-footnotes="1"><div class="footnotes"><div class="footnote" id="ft7683308-1"><a class="footnoterefnum" href="#ref7683308-1">[1]</a><div class="ftpara">Editor's Note: Former § 231-109, Final order, was repealed 4-16-2001 by Ord. No. 4.11.01.</div></div></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h3"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7683309 child"
      id="7683309"
      data-guid="7683309"
      data-parent-guid="7683279"
      data-position="5645"
      data-full-title="§ 231-110: Power to act in emergencies. "
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7683309_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7683309_label" for="7683309_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7683309"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 231-110
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7683309"
    >
Power to act in emergencies.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7683309" data-guid="7683309"></div>
        <div id="questions-7683309" data-guid="7683309" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7683309_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="history">[Amended <span class="legref" data-ref=""><span class="hisdate">4-16-2001</span> by <span class="loclaw">Ord. No. 4.11.01</span></span>]</div><div class="para">Whenever the chief officer of the Bureau at any stage of the proceedings instituted under the provisions of this code finds that a violation of this code exists which, in his or her opinion, requires immediate action to abate a direct hazard or immediate danger to the health, safety or welfare of the occupants of a building or of the public, he or she may, without prior notice or hearing, issue a notice and order, served in the manner provided in Chapter <a class="xref" guid="7681471" href="7681471#7681471">133A</a> of this Code, citing the violation and directing that such action be taken as is necessary to remove or abate the hazard or danger. Such order may include an order to vacate. Notwithstanding any other provision of this code, such an order shall be effective immediately upon service and shall be complied with immediately or as otherwise provided.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h3"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7683310 child"
      id="7683310"
      data-guid="7683310"
      data-parent-guid="7683279"
